            "descriptions": {
              "value": [
                {
                  "resource_id": "levelled_description",
                  "stats": {
                    "id": "levelled_description_c948901c63e6",
                    "level": {
                      "value": 1
                    },
                    "description": {
                      "value": "Your training focused on Crafting one particular kind of item. Select one of the specialties listed below; you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Crafting checks to Craft items of that type. If you are a master in Crafting, this bonus increases to +2.\n\nIf it's unclear whether the specialty applies, the GM decides. Some specialties might apply only partially. For example, if you were making a morningstar and had specialty in woodworking, the GM might give you half your bonus because the item requires both blacksmithing and woodworking.\n\nSpecialty | Applicable Items\nAlchemy* | Alchemical items such as elixirs\nArtistry | Fine art, including jewelry\nBlacksmithing | Durable metal goods, including metal armor\nBookmaking | Books and paper\nGlassmaking | Glass, including glassware and windows\nLeatherworking | Leather goods, including leather armor\nPottery | Ceramic goods\nShipbuilding | Ships and boats\nStonemasonry | Stone goods and structures\nTailoring | Clothing\nWeaving | Textiles, baskets, and rugs\nWoodworking | Wooden goods and structures"
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
